 ],
 "synopsis": "Madhur Iron & Steel (India) has refiled its draft papers with SEBI for an initial public offering comprising entirely a fresh issue of 1.1 crore equity shares. The issue size was increased from 1 crore shares planned in earlier draft papers filed in January 2026 and withdrawn in March 2026. The company, promoted by Jayant Agrawal, plans to use Rs 10 crore of the net proceeds to repay debt, Rs 81.95 crore to set up a manufacturing unit in Berla, Chhattisgarh, and Rs 34 crore for working capital requirements. Share India Capital Services is appointed as the book-running lead manager for the IPO.",
